{{!-- "Learning in public" — the newsletter ask, told as an
invitation rather than a subscription box. This is the FIRST
widget in the training sidebar: the page's whole promise is
"I'm working through this too", so the ask belongs at the top,
where the sponsor card used to sit.

Renders the inline members form when membership is on, and falls
back to a plain link to /signup/ when it isn't. --}}
<div class="widget widget-learn">
    <h4 class="widget-title">{{> "icons/signal"}} {{t "Learning in public"}}</h4>

    <p class="widget-learn-lead">{{t "I'm learning all of this myself — Salesforce, GTM, the AI tooling around it — and writing down every step as I go."}}</p>
    <p class="widget-learn-sub">{{t "Learn with me: I'll send what I learn straight to your inbox."}}</p>

    {{#if @site.members_enabled}}
        {{#unless @member}}
            <form class="signup-form widget-learn-form" data-members-form="signup">
                {{!-- .signup-row is not decoration: Ghost's success
                state hides it (.signup-form.success .signup-row), so
                dropping it would leave the input on screen after a
                successful subscribe. Stacked here by CSS, not markup. --}}
                <div class="signup-row">
                    <input class="signup-input" data-members-email type="email" required
                        placeholder="{{t "you@work-email.com"}}" aria-label="{{t "Your email"}}" />
                    <button class="btn btn-sm signup-btn" type="submit">{{> "icons/mail"}} {{t "Learn with me"}}</button>
                </div>
                <p class="signup-note">{{t "Free forever · unsubscribe in one click"}}</p>
                <p class="signup-success">{{> "icons/check-circle"}} {{t "Almost in! Check your inbox."}}</p>
                <p class="signup-error" data-members-error></p>
            </form>
        {{else}}
            <p class="widget-learn-sub">{{> "icons/check-circle"}} {{t "You're on the list — see you in your inbox."}}</p>
        {{/unless}}
    {{else}}
        <a class="btn btn-sm" href="{{@site.url}}/signup/">{{> "icons/mail"}} {{t "Learn with me"}}</a>
    {{/if}}
</div>
